repository-code: ""
abstract: >-
  Replication package for "SMEs and Public Procurement: the Costs of
  Restricting Tenders." This paper exploits a quasi-experimental variation
  from a program incentivizing the restriction of public tenders to SMEs
  in Sao Paulo, Brazil, to estimate the costs of this policy using a
  difference-in-differences in reverse (DiDiR) design. The code reproduces
  all 18 tables and 15 figures in the paper.
keywords:
  - public procurement
  - SMEs
  - difference-in-differences
  - policy evaluation
  - Brazil
  - replication
